LUAC(1)                     User Commands                    LUAC(1)

NAME
    luac - Lua 5.5 compiler

SYNOPSIS
    luac [options] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    luac translates Lua source files into one file of precompiled chunks,
    which lua(1) loads faster than source. Running the output is the same
    as running the given files in order. Source and precompiled files may
    be mixed. The output is not portable to other architectures or Lua
    releases, so the sources must be kept.

OPTIONS
    -l            list the bytecode; -l -l lists it in full. Without
                  files luac lists luac.out
    -o file       write the output to file instead of luac.out; - is the
                  standard output
    -p            only load the files, for syntax checks; nothing is
                  written
    -s            strip debugging information (line numbers and local
                  names) from the output
    -v            print the version
    --            stop handling options
    -             stop handling options and read the standard input

SEE ALSO
    lua(1)
